### Tested versions

- Reproducible on v4.7 (master)

### System information

Godot v4.7.dev (ebc126193) - cpe:/o:nixos:nixos:26.05 #1-NixOS SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sat Jan 17 15:31:30 UTC 2026 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Intel(R) Graphics (ADL GT2) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1240P (16 threads) - 15.33 GiB memory

### Issue description

(Please forgive the bad plotting from my WIP demo example in the MRP).
<img width="1024" height="543" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/af5cc23e-4a18-44cf-8a77-b8e136264549" />

After a huge amount of hacking and printing of array values I managed to recreate the bad calculation in Python, which is due to a bug in the [Hann Window](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_function#Hann_window) on [Line 116 of audio_effect_spectrum_analyzer.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/servers/audio/effects/audio_effect_spectrum_analyzer.cpp#L116) 

Basically there is a confusion due to a doubling of the size of the fft_size (beyond the doubling necessary to represent complex numbers and the doubling for the two stereo channels) resulting in the cosine wave being doubled.

Paste the following code into Jupyter Notebooks to plot these graphs.

```Python
%matplotlib inline
import math
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

freq = 44100; Hz = 440.0; N = 4096; phase = 0.85

def window_correct(x):
    return -0.5*math.cos(x*2*math.pi)+0.5
yval_correct = [ math.sin(2*math.pi*(i*Hz/freq+phase))*window_correct(i/(N-1))  for i in range(N) ]
plt.plot(yval_correct[:])
```

<img width="1089" height="799" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc707bb6-9ec4-4857-8bb1-e3fe77900260" />

```Python
def window_wrong(x):
    return -0.5*math.cos(2*x*2*math.pi)+0.5
yval_wrong = [ math.sin(2*math.pi*(i*Hz/freq+phase))*window_wrong(i/(N-1))  for i in range(N) ]
plt.plot(yval_wrong[:])
```

<img width="1089" height="799" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5c97982-90b4-407e-81b9-ba60ece41c2e" />


